Q: How can I prevent duplicate JSON-LD schema output in WordPress? A: <p>If Rank Math is already generating the <code>LocalBusiness</code> entity, I would not output a second independent <code>LocalBusiness</code> block for the same business.</p>
<p>The cleaner approach is to modify Rank Math's existing schema graph using its filters. Rank Math provides <code>rank_math/json_ld</code> specifically for adding or modifying data in the generated JSON-LD.</p>
<p>For example:</p>
<pre><code>add_filter( 'rank_math/json_ld', function ( $data, $jsonld ) {

    if ( ! is_page( 'example-service' ) ) {
        return $data;
    }

    foreach ( $data as $key =&gt; $schema ) {
        if (
            isset( $schema['@type'] ) &amp;&amp;
            in_array( $schema['@type'], [ 'LocalBusiness', 'Organization' ], true )
        ) {
            $data[ $key ]['telephone'] = '+1-555-555-5555';
            $data[ $key ]['priceRange'] = '$$';
        }
    }

    return $data;

}, 99, 2 );
</code></pre>
<p>The exact array structure should first be checked in Rank Math's generated JSON-LD, since the entity may not always be stored under the same key.</p>
<p>Having multiple <code>LocalBusiness</code> entities is valid when they actually represent different businesses or locations. I would avoid using two entities to describe the same business unless they are deliberately connected with consistent <code>@id</code> references.</p>
<p>So in this case my preference would be:</p>
<p><strong>Rank Math remains the owner of the main Organization/LocalBusiness entity, and custom code extends that entity.</strong></p>
<p>I would only disable Rank Math's entity and generate the complete schema myself if I needed full control over the entire graph. Otherwise you end up maintaining information that Rank Math is already maintaining for you.</p>
<p>Also, separate <code>&lt;script type=&quot;application/ld+json&quot;&gt;</code> blocks are not inherently a problem. The issue is duplicate/conflicting entities, not the number of JSON-LD script elements.</p>
